DESCRIPTION;LANGUAGE=en-US:Dear all\,\n\nJoin us for a very interesting dis
 cussion at this CPDSE Connect: "When AI Can Teach Anything\, Why Should St
 udents Show Up?"\n\n[cid:image001.jpg@01DCF3F7.58AB8660]\n\nQuestions that
  we will explore:\n\n1.    AI as a teaching tool: "Name one thing AI/DS ha
 s genuinely improved in your teaching — and one situation where you thin
 k we should not use it at all."\n\n2.     Growing data science: "How do yo
 u make your teaching compelling enough that students actually show up —
 when everything they need can be found in books\, AI\, or online?"\n\n3.
   Making data science accessible: "How are your students actually using AI
  — in class and in assignments — and how are you responding to it?"\n\
 n4.    Collaborative teaching: "What is good teaching in an AI/DS-heavy wo
 rld — and are we protecting enough space for the human\, interpersonal s
 ide of learning?"\n\n5.     Future CPDSE Connect format: "Design your idea
 l 30-minute CPDSE Connect meeting — and tell us what you need CPDSE to d
 o more of in the coming year."\n\nThe meeting will only be online.\n\nLook
 ing forward to connecting with you.\n\nBest regards\,\nFinn Kollerup\, Jac
 ob Fredegaard Hansen & Jeppe Hartmann\n___________________________________
 _____________________________________________\nMicrosoft Teams meeting\nJo
 in: https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/34227852967376?p=anuZpRM7dglD9GTlO4\n
